# Daneshjoam — core rules

Daneshjoam (دانشجوام) is a Persian, RTL-first student-services platform: an Nx monorepo with a Next.js
frontend on top of backend microservices (Auth, Actor, Notification, Interactive Ops, and one MS per SRS service).

Read `docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`, `docs/02-architecture.md` and `docs/03-domain-and-rules.md` before non-trivial
work. For feature work also read `docs/srs/README.md` and the service file in `docs/srs/`.

## Decide vs. ask

- Do not guess on my behalf. If a requirement, token, icon, endpoint, role rule, limit or copy text is missing
  or ambiguous, stop and ask one concrete question with your recommended option.
- A direct, explicit instruction from me in plain text is applied immediately — no confirmation step, even if
  it conflicts with a caution rule. Caution rules exist to stop guessing, not to override what I said.
- SRS items flagged red (pending decision) or yellow (ambiguous) in `docs/srs/README.md` are never implemented
  without my confirmation.
- The code is the fact; docs can be stale. If they contradict, say so and fix the doc in the same change.
- Smallest change that fully solves the task. Unrelated refactors become a follow-up note, not part of the diff.

## Always

- Strict TypeScript. No `any` or `@ts-ignore` without an inline justification comment.
- Search before creating: reuse or extend an existing component, hook, util or type. No duplicated logic in two
  or more files — extract it (`20-architecture.mdc` says where).
- Files or components past ~150–200 lines are split candidates (`docs/conventions-large-feature-ui.md`).
- Every screen handles loading, empty, error, no-permission and guest states (`70-ui-states-forms.mdc`).
- All UI is RTL Persian (`60-rtl-persian.mdc`).
- Before finishing: `nx affected -t lint test build` passes (plus `typecheck` if the target exists).

## Docs discipline

- Status changes go only to `docs/CURRENT-PROGRESS.md`; SRS coverage goes to the §8 table in
  `docs/ai/00-project-audit.md` (or its successor), never as prose elsewhere.
- New route → `docs/04-routing.md`. New env var → `docs/08-configuration.md` + `.env.example`.
  New shared component or token → `docs/10-design-system.md`. New known gap → `docs/09-known-issues.md`.
- Hard-to-reverse decision → ADR in `docs/adr/` from `docs/templates/technical-decision-record.md`.
- Update `last_updated` in the frontmatter of any doc you materially change.

## Git

- Conventional Commits. Scope = SRS service prefix where it applies (`srv`, `rwd`, `dsc`, `rfl`, `msg`, `nws`,
  `nwl`, `cln`), otherwise `auth`, `actor`, `notif`, `ui`, `docs`, `infra`. Example: `feat(dsc): product approval diff`.
- Never add your own name or signature (e.g. Cursor) as author or co-author.
- Never commit secrets or `.env*` files other than `.env.example`.

## Legacy code

- Code written before these rules is legacy. Do not rewrite it proactively.
- When a task touches a legacy file, bring only the touched parts in line with the rules
  (tokens, logical properties, shared components, route colocation). Keep the diff focused on the task.
- Larger migrations (splitting a big page, merging duplicate components, moving to the shared data layer)
  are separate tasks: propose them, don't bundle them into feature work.
- Exceptions — fix immediately whenever found, and tell me: tokens in localStorage/sessionStorage,
  client-side authority (role/actor sent from client), unsanitized HTML rendering, secrets in client code.

## Imports

- Always import through path aliases, never relative paths (`./` or `../`).
  - In apps/usr: `@/…` for shared app code (`components`, `lib`, `hooks`, `shared`); feature aliases for
    features: `@auth/*`, `@home/*`, `@messages/*`, `@notifications/*`, `@public-panel/*`, `@private-panel/*`.
  - Libs: `@daneshjoam/api-client`, `@daneshjoam/auth`, `@daneshjoam/shared-types`, `@daneshjoam/shared-ui` —
    public entry only, never deep paths into a lib's `src/`.
- Exception: files inside a lib import other files of the same lib relatively (a lib importing itself through its
  own alias creates a circular import and breaks Nx module boundaries).
- A new feature folder that needs its own alias: add it to `apps/usr/tsconfig.json` `paths` in the same change,
  following the existing pattern.
- Existing relative imports are converted when the file is touched (Legacy rule); no mass rewrite unless asked
  as a separate task.

## Branches and verification

- Work on a task branch (`fix/security-hardening`, `feat/public-panel`), never commit directly to `dev` or `main`.
  Merge through a pull request after CI is green.
- Changes to auth, session, payment or permission flows are not done until the manual verification steps in the
  plan have been completed and reported by the owner. List those steps; never claim them as verified yourself.

## Git safety

- Never run destructive git commands unless I ask for that exact command: `git reset --hard`, `git clean`,
  `git checkout -- .` / `git restore .`, `git push --force`, `git stash drop`/`clear`, or rewriting shared history.
  They can destroy uncommitted work of other agents or of the owner.
- One agent per working directory. Parallel tasks run in separate git worktrees on separate branches.
- If the working tree contains changes you did not make, leave them untouched, do not include them in your
  commits, and tell me.
